.TH BLASTEM 6 "September 2026" "BlastEm 0.6.3-pre" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
blastem \- emulator for Sega 8-bit and 16-bit systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blastem
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ ROMFILE
.RI [ WIDTH
.RI [ HEIGHT ]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B BlastEm
emulates the Sega Genesis and Mega Drive, Sega and Mega CD, 32X, Master
System and Mark III, Game Gear, SG-1000, and SC-3000 systems. When no ROM is
supplied, BlastEm opens its graphical game browser.
.PP
The optional
.I WIDTH
and
.I HEIGHT
arguments set the initial display dimensions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Display command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BI \-b " FRAMES"
Run headlessly and exit after the specified number of frames.
.TP
.B \-d
Enter the native debugger on startup. Use
.B \-dm
to debug the menu.
.TP
.B \-D
Enter the remote GDB debugger on startup.
.TP
.BI \-e " FILE|HOST:PORT"
Write a hardware event log to
.IR FILE ,
or stream it to the specified network endpoint.
.TP
.B \-f
Toggle fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B \-g
Disable OpenGL rendering and use the SDL renderer.
.TP
.B \-l
Log executed 68000 code addresses.
.TP
.BI \-m " MACHINE"
Force the emulated machine type. Recognized identifiers are
.BR gen ,
.BR sms ,
.BR gg ,
.BR sg ,
.BR sc ,
.BR 32x ,
.BR 32xcd ,
.BR pico ,
.BR copera ,
.BR jag ,
.BR media ,
and
.BR laser .
.TP
.B \-n
Disable the emulated Z80 processor.
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE"
Load
.I FILE
as a lock-on cartridge.
.TP
.BI \-r " J|U|E"
Force the region to Japan, USA, or Europe, respectively.
.TP
.BI \-s " FILE"
Load a GST-format save state from
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-t
Do not open a terminal window for the native debugger.
.TP
.B \-v
Display the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-y
Log individual YM-2612 channels to WAVE files.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/blastem/blastem.cfg
Per-user configuration. If absent, BlastEm reads the packaged default.
.TP
.I /usr/share/blastem/default.cfg
Packaged default configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/blastem
Runtime databases, controller mappings, interface images, and shaders.
.SH ROMS AND FIRMWARE
No commercial game ROMs, Sega firmware, or BIOS images are included. Users
must supply legally obtained game software and any optional firmware. The
graphical browser and the default emulated model do not require firmware.
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://www.retrodev.com/blastem
.SH BUGS
Report upstream BlastEm issues at
https://www.retrodev.com/blastem/trac/report.
